## Quick Start

```
1. rebrew todo --json                          # get highest ROI action items
2. rebrew lib-match --lib <runtime>.LIB --va 0x<VA>   # is it already in a library?
3. rebrew skeleton 0x<VA>                      # only for an inventory VA without source
4. rebrew test src/{target_name}/<func>.c --json  # compile + compare
5. # iterate code until STATUS: EXACT or RELOC
6. rebrew test --all --json                    # batch promote all ready functions
```

Check library attribution before implementing a function. Use `rebrew flirt`,
`rebrew crt-match`, and whole-body `rebrew lib-match` against the linked archive
when available. A signature miss is inconclusive. Library bytes contribute to
accounted `.text`, but library functions do not count as reversing progress.

## CLI Tools

Invoke routine tools through the single `rebrew <command>` CLI. Names such as
`rebrew-workflow` identify skills, not executables. Only `rebrew-cmake-cl`,
`rebrew-cmake-link`, `rebrew-cmake-lib`, and `rebrew-objdiff-build` are separate
build hooks, invoked by CMake/objdiff with their own arguments.
Use `--json` for structured output (preferred for agents).

